+# Contributing to Loru
+
+Thanks for helping improve Loru. This repository is designed so the core smoke path can be developed and tested offline on Python 3.11+.
+
+## Set up a development environment
+
+### macOS / Linux
+
+```bash
+python -m venv .venv
+source .venv/bin/activate
+pip install -e ".[dev,gui]"
+```
+
+### Windows PowerShell
+
+```powershell
+python -m venv .venv
+.\.venv\Scripts\activate
+pip install -e ".[dev,gui]"
+```
+
+The GUI extra is useful for desktop changes. For CLI/core-only work, `pip install -e ".[dev]"` is sufficient.
+
+## Run the verification commands
+
+Before opening a PR, run the repository's documented development checks:
+
+```bash
+pytest -q
+ruff check src tests
+loru demo
+```
+
+For GUI work, also launch `loru-gui`. If your change affects screenshots, refresh them with:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/capture_gui_shots.py
+```
+
+## Good-first-issue workflow
+
+1. Pick a small open bounty or good-first issue whose acceptance criteria you can reproduce locally.
+2. Keep the patch scoped to that issue; avoid unrelated refactors.
+3. Add or update tests when behavior changes.
+4. Run the verification commands above and include the relevant output in the PR description.
+5. Link the issue from the PR with `Fixes #N` when the PR fully resolves it.
+
+## MergeOS bounty claim flow
+
+Loru's funded tasks use the MergeOS MRG program. Before claiming a bounty:
+
+1. Follow the `mergeos-bounties` organization.
+2. Star `mergeos-bounties/mergeos`.
+3. Star `mergeos-bounties/mergeos-contracts`.
+4. Comment `I claim this bounty` on the Loru issue.
+5. Comment on MergeOS Claim Token #1 with a link to the Loru issue.
+6. Open the PR against Loru's `master` branch and include `Fixes #N`.
+
+The repository bounty policy is the source of truth for claim and payout rules: [`docs/BOUNTY.md`](docs/BOUNTY.md).
+
+## Pull request checklist
+
+- [ ] The PR is scoped to one issue/bounty or clearly explains why not.
+- [ ] `pytest -q` passes.
+- [ ] `ruff check src tests` passes.
+- [ ] `loru demo` passes for core/CLI changes.
+- [ ] GUI behavior is checked when the GUI is affected.
+- [ ] New datasets/media include license and consent notes where applicable.
+- [ ] Documentation and examples reflect changed behavior.
+- [ ] The PR description includes verification evidence and `Fixes #N` when applicable.
+
+## Data and accessibility care
+
+Loru handles sign-language data. Respect consent, privacy, licensing, and community context for any real recordings or derived datasets. Do not commit private recordings or redistribute media without permission. Synthetic/offline fixtures are preferred for deterministic tests.
